NTS: request at least four cookies in every NTS request

Each authenticated request spends one cookie and carries one placeholder
per further cookie wanted back; chronyd asks only for the cookies it is
missing, so with a full store (8) a request carries no placeholders.
The NTS servers of PTB (ptbtime1.ptb.de) and BEV (time.metrologie.at)
silently drop requests with fewer than three placeholders, i.e. requests
too small for a response with four cookies.  With stock chronyd they
answer one request in four (the store drops to four cookies, the request
then carries three placeholders and is answered, and the store is full
again), and the source stays unselectable for minutes.  With at least
four cookies requested, every request is answered and both servers are
selected 11-12 s after boot.  Surplus cookies are discarded by
extract_cookies() when the store is full.  Requests and responses grow
by three placeholders (about 312 bytes with PTB's 100-byte cookies).

Applied to src/ by "make update-chrony".

diff --git a/nts_ntp_client.c b/nts_ntp_client.c
index 3b92d1a..1bb8940 100644
--- a/nts_ntp_client.c
+++ b/nts_ntp_client.c
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@ NNC_GenerateRequestAuth(NNC_Instance inst, NTP_Packet *packet,
   inst->num_cookies--;
   inst->cookie_index = (inst->cookie_index + 1) % NTS_MAX_COOKIES;
 
-  req_cookies = MIN(NTS_MAX_COOKIES - inst->num_cookies,
+  req_cookies = MIN(MAX(NTS_MAX_COOKIES - inst->num_cookies, 4),
                     MAX_TOTAL_COOKIE_LENGTH / (cookie->length + 4));
 
   if (!NEF_AddField(packet, info, NTP_EF_NTS_UNIQUE_IDENTIFIER,
